 {"id":"fabro-b11a","title":"GRILL SESSION: how should fabro use the Chisel artifacts (cartography codebase map + quality calibration)? NOT for autonomous implementation","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T12:05:11.894Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T12:05:30.211Z","description":"This seed schedules a grill-with-docs session with the USER (user + agent). It must NEVER be picked by the develop workflow — it is blocked by the sentinel fabro-grill-gate (see below), so it stays out of 'sd ready'.\n\nContext: .chisel/ contains two artifact sets committed by upstream maintainer Bryan Helmkamp (2026-07-27, pre-world-merger): (1) cartography/ — an evidence-cited component map of the whole codebase (2256 files, purpose/paths/entry points/ownership/dependencies per component, codebase-map.md + .json + work/ analyses); (2) calibration/ — a 4-lens quality scoring (ownership/boundaries, simplicity, domain model, duplication of knowledge) run by 3 independent GPT-5 Codex reviewers + adjudication. Chisel itself is a private/unreleased tool (research 2026-09-07: no public repo/product found).\n\nGrill questions (to be worked in session with evidence: .chisel artifacts, ADRs 0009-0017, revisor reviews, codebase-design vocabulary):\nQ1 Should the cartography map feed the revisor/deepening phases as a structural input (replacing re-derivation), given it is pre-merger stale?\nQ2 Should we re-run/refresh the map (manually? via what tooling, since Chisel is not public?) or treat it as a point-in-time reference only?\nQ3 Do the calibration scores (fabro-workflow 2s on simplicity/duplication) set priorities for improve-codebase-architecture cycles?\nQ4 Lifecycle: keep upstream-synced (refresh on upstream merges), or fork-local ownership in .chisel/?\nQ5 Does any of this change how OUR reviews work (rust-style-guide axis vs chisel lenses)?\n\nOutcome of the session: decisions recorded (ADR if pivotal), separate implementation seeds filed for whatever is actionable, this seed closed, and the sentinel dependency removed. DO NOT IMPLEMENT ANYTHING from this seed in the autonomous line before the session happened.","labels":["grill","needs-user","decision"],"blockedBy":["fabro-919b"]}
 {"id":"fabro-919b","title":"SENTINEL (do not close): manual grill-session gate — permanently blocked by design","status":"open","type":"task","priority":4,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T12:05:25.947Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T12:06:11.357Z","description":"Permanent blocker gate for grill-session seeds that must NOT be autonomously implemented (user directive 2026-09-07). Mechanics: this sentinel is mutually blocked by its lock partner fabro-80cc (sd silently rejects self-dependencies, verified 2026-09-07), so both stay out of 'sd ready' forever. Any seed depending on this sentinel is likewise hidden from the planner until its dependency edge is removed. DO NOT close this sentinel, DO NOT remove any sentinel-pair edge. Usage: grill-session seeds add 'sd dep add <id> fabro-919b'; when the session concludes: 'sd dep remove <session-id> fabro-919b', file outcome seeds, close the session seed. Reusable for future grill sessions.","labels":["grill","needs-user","sentinel"],"blocks":["fabro-b11a","fabro-80cc"],"blockedBy":["fabro-80cc"]}
 {"id":"fabro-80cc","title":"SENTINEL LOCK PARTNER (do not close): mutual blocker for fabro-919b grill gate","status":"open","type":"task","priority":4,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T12:06:01.751Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T12:06:05.649Z","description":"Permanent lock partner for fabro-919b. These two sentinels block EACH OTHER (mutual dependency cycle), so both are permanently hidden from 'sd ready' and can never be picked by the develop workflow. sd silently rejects self-dependencies (verified 2026-09-07), which is why the gate needs a partner seed instead. DO NOT close either sentinel, DO NOT remove either dependency edge. Grill-session seeds depend on fabro-919b; when a session concludes, only remove the SESSION seed's edge (sd dep remove <session-seed> fabro-919b) — the sentinel pair stays locked forever and is reusable for future grill sessions.","labels":["grill","needs-user","sentinel"],"blocks":["fabro-919b"],"blockedBy":["fabro-919b"]}
-{"id":"fabro-5e09","title":"Develop planner: pick only seeds assigned to fabro (sd ready --assignee fabro) — deterministic line/user ownership split","status":"in_progress","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T12:16:32.837Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:04:02.166Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"USER CORRECTION 2026-09-07 (governance): the LINE implements only the MECHANISM; WHICH seeds belong to the line is a USER decision, never a bulk heuristic run by the line itself.\n\nMECHANISM (line implements): (1) develop planner prompt (.fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md) candidate source becomes 'sd ready --assignee fabro --limit 200' — CLI pre-filters, the LLM never sees seeds not assigned to fabro (data-level determinism); (2) goal fast-path honors a named seed id ONLY when assignee is fabro; (3) claim step: 'sd update <id> --status in_progress --assignee fabro'; (4) Tracker-empty on the FILTERED view = legitimate end of work (park), not a broken tracker — FAIL-CLOSED: while the backlog is unassigned the line does nothing rather than something; (5) docs/agents/issue-tracker.md documents the convention: assignee is the ownership switch; filers assign at creation; the user can reassign/unassign anytime as veto.\n\nOWNERSHIP (user decides, NOT this seed's implementer): the existing backlog assignment list is prepared by the agent as a proposal, reviewed and approved by the USER in chat (or the pending grill session), then applied from the user side. NO bulk-assign by the develop run. The sentinel pair (fabro-919b/fabro-80cc) stays in place until the mechanism lands AND the user has curated the backlog; retiring it is part of the user-approved migration, not this implementation.\n\nAcceptance: planner prompt ships the filtered command; a user-assigned open seed never appears in a develop run's candidates; empty filtered view parks; docs updated; ownership list untouched by the implementer.","labels":["workflows","revision"]}
